    details: [{ title: "Authenticate on your server", text: "Create an API key in Agents & API keys. Send it as Authorization: Bearer with requests under https://findmeadow.com/api/bridge. Keys have full workspace access and must not be exposed in public frontend code." }, { title: "Discover projects and accounts", text: "GET /projects identifies your projects. GET /projects/{projectId}/accounts lists connected destinations. Use the options endpoint to resolve account-specific choices such as TikTok privacy and Pinterest boards." }, { title: "Upload and reuse media", text: "The project media endpoints create reusable media IDs. Select a suitable upload route for the file size and wait for the media to be ready. Social platform file, format, and duration requirements still apply." }, { title: "Inspect delivery or subscribe to events", text: "GET /projects/{projectId}/posts/{postId} reports the post and delivery outcomes. Signed post.completed webhooks report a result per destination; connection.needs_reconnect reports an account that needs authorization again." }],
    guide: [{ title: "Use the API for a fixed workflow", text: "A release script, content pipeline, or internal service can construct the same items array each time. Give new submissions unique request IDs, handle HTTP failures, inspect preview errors, and track each delivery after submission. You can also save drafts for a person to review in Meadow." }, { title: "Keep your platform versions together", text: "Each item contains caption, title, format, mediaIds, accountIds, and optional schedule. Its overrides object is keyed by account ID. Override the destination’s caption, title, format, localDateTime, and settings only where that version needs to differ." }],
    noteHeading: "Workspace access is different from a platform API.", noteText: "Meadow’s API acts on your authorized Meadow workspace accounts. It is not a general wrapper for every platform operation, and it does not expose your social account credentials. The REST API uses Meadow API keys; an OAuth token issued for the MCP resource is not a REST credential.",
